UpdateConstructionDatesTest
├── when the property does not exist
│   └── it should revert with PropertyDoesNotExist
├── when the property exists
│   ├── when the caller is not the property issuer
│   │   └── it should revert with NotPropertyIssuer
│   ├── when the caller is the property issuer
│   │   ├── when the contract is paused
│   │   │   └── it should revert with EnforcedPause
│   │   └── when the contract is not paused
│   │       ├── when the property is not active
│   │       │   └── it should revert with PropertyNotActive
│   │       └── when the property is active
│   │           ├── when the new construction start is zero
│   │           │   └── it should revert with InvalidDates
│   │           ├── when the new estimated completion is zero
│   │           │   └── it should revert with InvalidDates
│   │           ├── when the new estimated completion is before or equal to construction start
│   │           │   └── it should revert with InvalidDates
│   │           ├── when the property status is Completed
│   │           │   └── it should revert with PropertyAlreadyCompleted
│   │           ├── when the property status is Sold
│   │           │   └── it should revert with PropertyAlreadyCompleted
│   │           └── when dates are valid and status allows updates
│   │               ├── when status is Planning
│   │               │   ├── it should update both dates
│   │               │   ├── it should emit ConstructionDatesUpdated event
│   │               │   └── it should preserve all other property data
│   │               ├── when status is InConstruction
│   │               │   ├── it should update both dates
│   │               │   ├── it should emit ConstructionDatesUpdated event
│   │               │   └── it should allow extending deadlines
│   │               └── when dates are the same as current
│   │                   └── it should update anyway (idempotence)

